WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We were talking backstage.
-Yeah.

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.335 line:92%
-The last time you were here,

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
was right before
your show started.

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
Yes, two years ago.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Two years ago.
And the other guest that night

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.275
was an up-and-coming politician
named Hillary Clinton.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And had you met her before?

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was the first time
I ever met her.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:16.349
And my friend Allana totally
rushed her in her dressing room

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
and made us
take a picture together.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's so blurry,
'cause we're all too excited.

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
I think that's nice.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
To have a photo so blurry
to show the moment is great.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.559 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Exactly. Yeah.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Compared to what
you thought it would be like

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what it's been like,
how has your show affected you

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.197 line:92%
over these last two years?

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:35.769
-Well, as a citizen, I would say
it's a similar experience,

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I thought
it was gonna be one way,

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it became another way.
-Yeah.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:43.043 line:92%
-But it's been a very wild ride.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:43.710 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It's been really fun,

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's been invigorating
and terrifying,

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:48.782 line:92%
and a lot of different things.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well that's good.
I certainly enjoy watching it.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
Another show
I really enjoy watching --

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.487 line:92%
You actually share a studio

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
with "Last Week Tonight,"
with John Oliver.

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.957
-I do, yes, we share a space.
-And you guys have obviously

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:58.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
known each other
for a long time.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, we have.
-You used to work together.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.295 line:92%
Sharing the same physical space,

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you ever leave notes
for one another?

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We never really
cross paths that much.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:09.269 size:78% position:39%
But I did actually --
I did engrave my --

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did engrave something
in his desk.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't know
if he knows that.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.706 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
I took, like --
I don't know.

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess I was randomly
holding a knife.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think, under his desk --
As one does.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:24.117
Under his desk somewhere, it
says, like, "Sam Bee was here."

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's great.
-Yeah.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What a fun thing
to find one day.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-And then probably

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
work backwards
to the same question of,

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:32.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Why does Sam have a knife?"
-It's been years.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I know.

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your show, obviously,
very hard on the president,

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
to a point
that some people believe

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
there is
something shady going on.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a bit
of a conspiracy theory

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.170 line:92%
out there about your show.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, my dad has a lot
of friends, who think that --

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have conspiracy theories
about me.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.343
They think that every time
I mention Hillary Clinton

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get $25.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:55.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which I do,
because we're best friends,

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.483 line:92%
but I'm sure you get that, too.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.284 size:88% position:44%
I mean, everybody thinks
that when you make jokes

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the typical comedy sphere,
that, like,

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
George Soros
provides you with...

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, it's so funny to me
that no one thinks

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.827
you can just come to these
conclusions independently...

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.396 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, no, no, no, no.
-...without cash reward.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:13.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's for a $25 per diem.
-Yeah.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just cruising along
with all that

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.671 line:92%
sweet, sweet George Soros cash.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.406 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And last Friday --

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you guys are off
for a little bit.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:22.475 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-We were.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:25.145
-'Cause obviously Friday --
We had to wait till today.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys
are gonna approach it

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
in two days, on Wednesday.
-I know.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to do it every day.
I'm so sorry.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, but I --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:32.852 line:92%
-I mean, like, no, it's good.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think
there are great difficulties

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
to doing it once a week,
as well.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:36.523 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, there are.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:39.192
I mean, you get to cover --
You get to do it every day.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think it's --
So much is --

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm trying to find
the right word for it.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:46.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
So much is [bleep] out
every day that...

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:46.566 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
...doing the show every day,
you're just like --

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're just running around
with a bucket.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.537 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure, totally.

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:51.638 line:92%
-Like, you're an actual plumber

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
who like might actually
fix the toilet.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:57.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We get the fire hose in the
face of feces, as well.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:57.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.944 --> 00:03:00.213 size:88% position:44%
-But we get to sit back
and kind of analyze for,

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
a couple of days at least.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:05.018
But, you know, there's a lot of
man things to talk about.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
You, uh...

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Not you.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, I know.
But there are --

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
Being on Team Man,
it's been a --

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like we're not a --
not a great week.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.429
We need to fire our coach
and hire a new GM or something.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know, you do.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But on Friday, obviously,
the plea deal happens.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And what is the reaction

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:25.238 line:92%
in the "Full Frontal" offices?

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:26.606 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh, well...

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.807 line:92%
Okay, there's a moment --

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.410
I guess,
when it comes to the plea deal,

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
it really is sad
what passes for joy.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:33.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Because you feel that --

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you're like,
"Oh, it's so exciting!"

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:38.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you're like,
"Every smile is joyless.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every piece of laughter
is mirthless."

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I remember I woke up
Friday morning,

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I listen to the
New York Times podcast,

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.660 size:84% position:42%
and they were really
intensely talking about

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.130
how the tax bill was like
a trillion dollars off.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I LOL'd.
I was like, "Ha ha ha!

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:56.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
A trillion dollars?!
Ha ha ha ha!

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, my God."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then --
And then, it passed.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:03.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really a trillion and a
half, don't worry.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.678 line:92%
-We listen to the same podcast.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:08.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
if you found this recently.

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:10.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The music
is very triggering now.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.184 line:92%
-The music is triggering.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:12.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's "The Daily."
It's fantastic.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes the news is so bad
that I just speed it up.

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:17.557
Like, I try to listen to it
just talking very fast, like,

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.425
"And now it looks like
Republicans will pass the bill,

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.293 line:92%
and it's gonna be $1.5 trillion.

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's gonna hurt
the middle class."

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:23.162
I'm like, "Oh, just get it out!
Just get it out!"

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:23.696 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:27.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't want to spend
a lot of time with this.

